# What NOT to upload to an EAS build.
#
# When this file exists EAS uses it INSTEAD of .gitignore. That is the whole
# reason it is here: src/config/secret.js is gitignored (the repository is
# public and the first API key had to be rotated after being published), but
# the app imports API_KEY from it at build time. Without this file the upload
# skips it and the build fails with "Cannot find module './secret'".
#
# So: keep secret.js OUT of git, and IN the build.

node_modules/
.expo/
dist/
web-build/
*.log
.DS_Store

# Local build output
android/
ios/

# Nothing below the app itself needs to reach a build server
../backend/
../ml-models/
../docs/
